Title: Right On Time
Credit: An original two-scene short for the Soundstage tutorial
Author: Jane Doe
Draft date: 2026-11-02

EXT. CANNERY STREET - NIGHT

Rain hammers an empty street of shuttered shops. A sodium lamp buzzes over the curb.

ROSA (30s, yellow rain jacket) waits under the lamp, a phone to her ear. A stack of wooden CRATES blocks the middle of the road.

ROSA
(into the phone)
Two minutes. He'd better be early.

Headlights flare at the far end of the street. Rosa turns to watch them come.

A red SPORTS CAR tears out of the rain, DEX (40s, leather jacket) at the wheel. It hits the crates dead center. Wood explodes across the wet road.

The car roars past her and is gone.

Rosa lowers the phone. Almost smiles.

ROSA
He's through.

CUT TO:

INT. SPORTS CAR (MOVING) - LATER

Rain streams down the windshield. Dex drives, both hands on the wheel. A splinter of crate is still caught in the wiper.

Rosa rides beside him, soaked, hood down.

DEX
You said two minutes.

ROSA
And you were early.

Dex grins. The street lamps slide past into the rain.